  <h1>How does Salesforce connect with third-party ERP systems?</h1>
  <p>
    In today’s digital era, businesses often use multiple systems to manage different operations efficiently. 
    Salesforce, being one of the most powerful CRM platforms, allows seamless integration with third-party ERP systems 
    such as SAP, Oracle, Microsoft Dynamics, and NetSuite. This integration bridges the gap between front-office 
    customer management and back-office business operations.
  </p>
  
  <p>
    Integrating Salesforce with ERP systems ensures real-time data synchronization, helping organizations manage 
    leads, sales orders, invoices, and financial transactions without manual intervention. APIs (Application 
    Programming Interfaces) and middleware tools such as MuleSoft, Dell Boomi, and Jitterbit play a vital role 
    in facilitating this integration. These tools help in connecting Salesforce with ERP systems by managing 
    data mapping, transformation, and workflow automation.
  </p>

  <div class="highlight">
